<section class="g-paper" id="doors">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal><span class="tick">\</span> 02 · Where most teams start</div>
    <h2 data-v9-reveal style="--d:60ms">Four front doors.</h2>
    <p class="lead" data-v9-reveal style="--d:120ms">
      Two decide who you hire. Two put the person on a payroll. Most stuck roles start with the first one.
    </p>
    <div class="sv-doors">
      <article class="sv-door" id="sv-scorecard" data-v9-reveal style="--d:0ms">
        <span class="sv-top"><span class="sv-kind">Advisory</span><span class="sv-no">No. 01</span></span>
        <h3>Role scorecard</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>You give us</dt><dd>45 minutes with the hiring manager.</dd><dt>You get</dt><dd>
            A scorecard everyone agrees on, and the interview guide that goes with it.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="sv-note">Most stuck searches are stuck here. Two days is enough to find out.</p>
        <i class="sv-perf" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <p class="sv-meta"><span>2 days</span><span>Fixed fee</span></p>
      </article>
      <article class="sv-door" id="sv-review" data-v9-reveal style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="sv-top"><span class="sv-kind">Assessment</span><span class="sv-no">No. 02</span></span>
        <h3>Pipeline review</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>You give us</dt><dd>The CVs you already turned down.</dd><dt>You get</dt><dd>
            A ranked shortlist, and whether you missed someone.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="sv-note">Sometimes the hire is already sitting in the pile you rejected.</p>
        <i class="sv-perf" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <p class="sv-meta"><span>5 days</span><span>Fixed fee</span></p>
      </article>
      <article class="sv-door" id="sv-perm" data-v9-reveal style="--d:160ms">
        <span class="sv-top"><span class="sv-kind">Recruitment</span><span class="sv-no">No. 03</span></span>
        <h3>Permanent hire</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>You give us</dt><dd>A role.</dd><dt>You get</dt><dd>
            Three scored candidates to interview. They join your payroll.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="sv-note">
          The right engagement for a role or two. Past a handful a year, managed hiring does the same job for less, and
          we’ll tell you on the first call.
        </p>
        <i class="sv-perf" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <p class="sv-meta"><span>About 36 hours to three</span><span>% of annual CTC, on hire</span></p>
      </article>
      <article class="sv-door" id="sv-contract" data-v9-reveal style="--d:240ms">
        <span class="sv-top"><span class="sv-kind">Contract to hire</span><span class="sv-no">No. 04</span></span>
        <h3>Contract hire</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>You give us</dt><dd>A skill gap and a duration.</dd><dt>You get</dt><dd>
            We find them and employ them. They work in your team.
          </dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="sv-note">Same scorecard and same expert interview as a permanent hire. Only the payroll changes.</p>
        <i class="sv-perf" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <p class="sv-meta"><span>Month by month</span><span>Monthly rate</span></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
